  "worked_solution": "To find the coordinates of the point, we inspect its position along the $x$ and $y$ axes.\n\nThe point is $4$ units to the *left* of the origin, in the *negative* direction of the $x$-axis. So, the point has an $x$-coordinate of $-4.$\n\nAdditionally, the point is $8$ units *below* the origin, in the *negative* direction of the $y$-axis. So, the point has a $y$-coordinate of $-8.$\n\nThe point has an $x$-coordinate of $-4$ and a $y$-coordinate of $-8,$ so its coordinates are $(-4,-8).$",
